{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888568,"nonce":"BLH3orvJVpGPdPnSNyu49PNXZkE=","title":"A human cannot draw an Incident from the Cases list, because /cases has no multi-select","message":"**What is wrong.** ADR 0052 §2 names a human as one of an Incident's two authors. `b2672a1` gives the API; `/cases` (`web/src/routes/cases.tsx`) offers no way to select several Cases and draw one, nor to add a Case to an existing Incident from case detail.\n\n**The demonstration.** On `/cases`, rows are single-click links; there is no selection state.\n\n**Why it matters.** Without it the only author in the UI is a Correlator, and the human path the owner ruled in is API-only.\n\n**Where.** `web/src/routes/cases.tsx` (multi-select + \"Draw Incident\"), `web/src/routes/case-detail.tsx` (\"Add to Incident…\", \"Move to Incident…\", showing the current Incident).\n\n**Scope.** small.\n\n**Done when.** A user selects Cases on `/cases` and draws an Incident that opens at `/incidents/{number}`; case detail shows the Case's Incident and offers add or move; selecting a Case already in an Incident shows that it will be moved, not duplicated; component tests cover selection, draw and move; `tsc` and `just ci` green.\n\n**Blocked by.** `b2672a1`\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}